WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.120
Ever wondered how to make a cool couple of
million dollars?

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.810
Well, one option would be to sharpen your
bidding skills and join the cast of Storage

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:07.340
Wars.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.780
Power couple Brandi Passante and Jarrod Schulz
have raked in a small fortune while bidding

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.240
on storage units for the A&amp;E reality show.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.700
The pair were original cast members on Storage
Wars, which first began in 2010.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.260
After this, they became so popular with fans
and producers alike that in 2014 they were

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.500
given their own spin-off, Brandi &amp; Jarrod:
Married to the Job which followed their lives

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.160
as they juggled their personal dealings with
their work.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.240
"Who are all these f------ people?”

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.340
“I had to throw my pool party in the front
yard.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.080
We got the taco guy over here."

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.550
Sadly, that spin-off lasted for only eight
episodes, and Passante and Schulz decided

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:42.160
not to continue for a second season.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:47.460
The two last appeared on the original Storage
Wars in March 2018, calling it quits after

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.060
11 seasons and many, many high-stakes bids.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:54.100
These days, the couple each maintain a much
lower profile having been able to give up

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:58.030
the spotlight thanks to the huge stacks of
cash they raked in during their time on Storage

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:58.520
Wars.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:02.400
But just how much money are Brandi Passante
and Jarrod Schulz worth today?

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.790
According to Celebrity Net Worth, Passante's
net worth hit the $2 million mark in 2019,

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.200
while Schulz is reportedly also worth approximately
$2 million.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:15.060
Of course, Brandi Passante and Jarrod Schulz
wouldn't be worth several millions dollars

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.660
today if they hadn't landed their roles on
Storage Wars.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:22.360
Their involvement on the beloved A&amp;E show
reportedly came after Schulz's aunt encouraged

00:01:22.360 --> 00:01:24.380
him to get into the storage auction business.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.270
At one auction, Schulz met the Storage Wars
producers, and eight months later they arrived

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.680
at his and Passante's antiques store to recruit
him.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:35.100
After subsequently meeting Passante, the same
producers decided to bring her in, too.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.680
Passante and Schulz's playful bickering quickly
won over fans of the show.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:42.680
In particular, Passante's bright demeanor
made her a firm fan favorite, while Schulz's

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:46.350
tendency towards impulsive bidding blended
well with his partner's more cautious brand

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:46.840
of buying.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:51.200
In fact, there's a good reason Passante kept
cautious while bidding on Storage Wars: because

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.380
Passante knew nothing about auctions before
she was cast.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.000
The whole game was more Schulz's wheelhouse,
but the Storage Wars producers recruited her

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.970
anyway, presumably because they were so taken
with the pair's chemistry.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.770
Obviously, it's clear that decision more than
paid off for both the show's team and for

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.660
Passante and Schulz themselves.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:12.760
In the early days of Storage Wars, the cast
was reportedly paid $2,000 per episode.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:17.140
As the show grew in popularity, however, those
salaries sky-rocketed, particularly for the

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.040
original cast.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:23.520
By the time Passante and Schulz left Storage
Wars, they were each earning $15,000 per episode.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.420
During their spin-off, it was reported that
Passante earned around $12,000 per episode.

00:02:28.420 --> 00:02:32.840
At the same time, Schulz was earning a total
of around $58,000 per month.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.970
Passante and Schulz's financial fortunes even
blossomed despite the fact that the second

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.760
branch of their Now and Then antiques store
never turned a profit.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:43.400
When the couple were recruited to the show,
they had already opened a store in Orange,

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:43.900
California.

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.760
During the pair's stint on the show, they
opened a second location in Long Beach.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.050
Sadly, since then, both stores have closed
down one in 2014 and one in early 2019.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.240
"This feels like some bad juju voodoo."

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.920
Beyond the show and their antiques stores,
much of the couple's success comes from their

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:02.120
other business ventures.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.460
For example, Passante and Schulz run another
store called Outlaw Apparel, which sells a

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:08.080
range of clothing and accessories.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:13.260
The store opened in 2009, a year before Storage
Wars started, with Schulz himself taking on

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.650
an important role in the design process for
much of the brand's clothing.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:20.921
Today, with Passante and Schulz seemingly
retired from the reality TV game, the couple

00:03:20.921 --> 00:03:23.340
seem to be enjoying a more low-key way of
life.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.700
Unfortunately, in 2019, Schulz stopped appearing
in Passante's Instagram posts, leading to

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.900
speculation that the couple may have split.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.030
Although this hasn't been confirmed, it'd
no doubt be a tragic end for one of reality

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.020
television's most successful couples.

